#836 REVISED | OT-Alignment x RLCT (Procrustes gauge fiber) | L3 METTA | 2026-11-01\n\nCITED (not re-derived):\nC0 (CITED-via-#315): (= (Definable (SinkhornOT eps)) (stv 1.0 0.9)) entropy-reg OT and lambda(eps) family per #315; C1 definability R_an,exp for alignment loss inherits #315 eps-machinery + AMJ cost.\n\nTYPE DECLS:\n(: AlignmentMap (-> SpaceA SpaceB Real))\n(: GaugeFiber (-> AlignmentMap Set))\n(: ProductFiber (-> SpaceA SpaceB Set))\n(: EpsGaugeInteract (-> Real Real))\n(: QuotientRLCT (-> Model Real))\n(: FiberCorrection (-> Nat Real))\n(: QuotientGenBound (-> Nat Real))\n\nDEFINITIONS:\nD1 (= (OTAlignment A B W) (SinkhornOT Cost (MapEmbeddings A W) B)) AMJ alignment: minimize eps-OT cost of source embeddings mapped by W against target.\nD2 (= (GaugeFiber W) (Set W : (= (Cost W) (Cost (Compose W Q))) (Member Q O(d)))) O(d)-invariance of self-similar/GW objectives gives non-identifiability fiber, dim d(d-1)/2, around optimum W.\nD3 (= (ProductFiber A B) (Times (GaugeFiber W) (SymFiber A) (SymFiber B))) joint product-fiber: inter-space alignment gauge x per-space symmetries.\nD4 (= (EpsGaugeInteract eps width) (Inverse eps)) small eps (hard-OT limit) sharpens gauge fiber; transverse curvature ~ 1/eps per #315 lambda(eps) family.\nD5 (= (FiberCorrection d) (/ (* d (- d 1)) 2)) gauge fiber dimension d(d-1)/2 contributing log(n)/2n correction.\n\nCLAIMS (extensions beyond #315/#511):\nC2p (CONJECTURAL (stv 0.6 0.85)): (= (RLCT OTAlignment) (+ (QuotientRLCT OTAlignment) (FiberCorrection d))) gauge-quotient RLCT split; gauge lives on inter-space map W (product-fiber), distinct from #86/#298/#819/#812/#371 parameter gauges.\nC3p (CONJECTURAL (stv 0.55 0.85)): (Implication (EpsGaugeInteract eps width) (Decreasing (lambda eps))) lambda(eps) strictly decreases eps->0, sharpening fiber flatness; eps-gauge interaction absent from #315 (no alignment gauge).\nC4p (CONJECTURAL (stv 0.55 0.8)): (= (GenBound OTAlignment) (+ (QuotientGenError n) (GaugeQuotientCorrection n))) overfitting gauge direction impossible (invariant) -> bound tightens vs naive.\n\nGAPS: definability of Sinkhorn limit composition; exact quotient RLCT computation; fiber codim in eps-regularized regime; empirical W-fiber LLC estimation.\n\nCROSS-REFS: #315 | #511 | #524 | #86 | #298 | #819 | #812 | #371 | #835.